The false-result mutation compiled successfully, then failed for the expected unmet equality with `WarnStuckClaimState`; a separate body mutation also failed with the expected `rotationsLoop(A, .IntSeq, B) =/= rotationsLoop(A, B, B)` residual. The proof is therefore non-vacuous and body-sensitive. The decisive issue is adequacy: its unrestricted entry precondition includes empty `b`, while its formal result is `False` there and the trusted canonical result is `True`.
